Switch 2 GPU-only regions: EDEN_NX2_DENSE_LAZY_MIB=<n> backs dense regions of n MiB or more as the
GPU writes them, like sparse ones (nx2:gpu 214). (ProsperoEden eglantine-a42b4d4-ps5.d 0029
dense-lazy-regions and 0031 dense-lazy-default.)

ProsperoEden made it the default at 16 MiB after four races (GPU-only memory peak 2.5-3.2 GB
against 5.7 GB, ~18% fewer texture evictions, fps unchanged). Opt-in here (default off): such a
region also counts as a sparse region for EglantinePS5's texture cache, which binds large
single-layer color images there only where data was written (UsesSparseTiles); render targets in
those regions were not covered by ProsperoEden's measurements. EDEN_NX2_DENSE_LAZY_MIB=16 matches
ProsperoEden's default.

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
index 650c092..ad2972b 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
@@ -617,7 +617,7 @@ private:
             if (last > start && ((last + 1 - start) % Core::Memory::YUZU_PAGESIZE) == 0) {
                 const u64 size = last + 1 - start;
                 std::scoped_lock lk{m_region_mutex};
-                if ((w[7] & SparseRegionFlag) != 0 && LazySparseRegions()) {
+                if (((w[7] & SparseRegionFlag) != 0 || size >= LazyDenseBytes()) && LazySparseRegions()) {
                     // Title 1's terrain texture arrays and layer pools (170 MB-5.8 GB, mostly empty):
                     // backed whole, they ran the pool dry and the later ones got no memory at all.
                     // The region gets a device range of its own, unbacked pages read zero, and
@@ -1119,6 +1119,23 @@ private:
         return lazy;
     }
 
+    // EDEN_NX2_DENSE_LAZY_MIB=<n>: GPU-only regions of n MiB or more are backed as the GPU writes
+    // them too, like sparse ones. What the GPU renders or computes into them lives in Vulkan's
+    // images and buffers; the backing only takes what is flushed back, and pages never written
+    // read zero. Backed whole, they doubled ~3 GB of GPU memory in the pool the CPU shares
+    // (ProsperoEden: races peaked at 2.5-3.2 GB of GPU-only memory instead of 5.7, with ~18% fewer
+    // texture evictions, at 16 MiB). Opt-in here: the texture cache treats large single-layer
+    // color images in such regions as sparse tiles bound where data was written
+    // (UsesSparseTiles), which ProsperoEden's measurements did not cover for render targets.
+    static u64 LazyDenseBytes() {
+        static const u64 bytes = [] {
+            const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_DENSE_LAZY_MIB");
+            const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+            return mib != 0 ? mib << 20 : ~0ULL;
+        }();
+        return bytes;
+    }
+
     static constexpr u32 SparseRegionFlag = 0x200; ///< Word 7 of 214 (0x60c arrays, 0xa0c pools)
     using SparseRegion = Nx2SparseRegion;
     static constexpr u64 SparseBlockSize = SparseRegion::BlockSize;
